{
  "_comment": "Known, accepted CVEs as of the review date below, tracked so CI blocks on any NEW vulnerability without silently ignoring the whole scan. Most entries here require a major-version bump (langgraph 0.2->1.x, langchain-core 0.3->1.x, streamlit 1.40->1.53+, starlette->1.x) that would need its own dedicated upgrade + regression pass, not a drive-by dependency bump. 2026-09-11 review added three CVEs from the Phase 3 dependency additions, all confirmed unreachable in this codebase and all locked behind the same langgraph 0.2->1.x / langchain 0.3->1.x major bump: langgraph-checkpoint-postgres PYSEC-2026-3635 (namespace LIKE-prefix leak in the BaseStore search/list_namespaces API -- AgentIQ uses AsyncPostgresSaver for checkpoints keyed by exact thread_id, never the Store namespace API); langsmith PYSEC-2026-2555 (unsafe deserialization of prompt manifests via pull_prompt/hub.pull -- all prompts here are inline string constants, never pulled from the Hub); langsmith CVE-2026-59152 (arbitrary file read via langsmith's ASGI TracingMiddleware -- not installed; tracing here is the env-var callback, off by default with no LANGCHAIN_API_KEY on the deployed instances). Re-run scripts/check_pip_audit.py --update-baseline after actually upgrading a package, and prune entries that no longer apply. 2026-11-04 review added langgraph-checkpoint-postgres CVE-2026-115883 (dotted namespace labels reach another tenant's data through the store API; fixed in 3.1.3, which needs the langgraph 0.2->1.x major bump); not reachable here, since AgentIQ uses the checkpointer keyed by thread and never the store or namespace API.",
  "reviewed_date": "2026-11-04",
